From 67a2329a9c743f9be5c45315c0ac1d9dd2cacabd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Fr=C3=A9d=C3=A9ric=20B=C3=A9rat?= <fberat@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Dec 2025 20:26:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Improve package committish resolution logic

Centralizes and corrects how package committish (branch/tag/commit) is
determined for various package types and configurations.

This change addresses inconsistencies in branch determination, incorrect
EPEL chroot string formatting, and missing parameters in
`get_last_build` for reverse dependencies.

- Refactored `MpbPackage.collect_build_info` to improve clarity and
  accuracy of committish resolution.
- Introduced `MpbBackend.get_distgit_branch` to centralize logic for
  retrieving default branches based on distgit and release version.
- Corrected the EPEL chroot string format from `el{release}` to
  `epel{release}`.
- Ensured `is_revdep` is correctly passed to
  `MpbWhatrequires.get_last_build` when retrieving build info for
  reverse dependencies.
- Refined `@last_build` committish handling to accurately set a value
  only if a valid last build is found.
- Updated `revdep_branch` formatting to consistently apply `releasever`
  from metalinks configurations.
- Added debug logging for resolved committish values in `MpbPackage`.
- Updated CI regression tests (`006-copr.sh`, `007-info.gl.sh`) to
  thoroughly validate the new branch resolution logic for main and
  reverse dependency packages, including specific EPEL scenarios, and
  improved test output for clarity.
- Commented out an example `branch` setting in `epel.yaml`.
